<title>INDIA: India BPL 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India BPL 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		484.7     vs     473.3</p>
<p>    Sales		 12,906.0	vs   11,803.8</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	  3.0	vs	  3.0</p>
<p>    Tax			128.1	vs	135.0</p>
<p>    Profit before tax    612.8	vs	608.3</p>
<p>Note: BPL Ltd is a consuemr appliance manufacturer. The firm said the volume of its domestic sales of colour televisions increased 10.6 percent even though the market size remained static at 1.8 million colour televisions. The firm's black-and-white television sales grew 35 percent, it added.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
